Wild garlic pest[o] is very easy to make. You will need wild garlic[,] grated par[mes]an cheese[,] pine nuts, olive oil,[ lemon] juice[ and] salt & pepper. Simply place all ingredients in a food processor and blitz until you get the desired consistency. You can[ add] more olive oil to the mixture if needed.
This luxury shrimp pasta[ dish] is[ very] easy and quick to make. It is ready in just 20 minutes, and you can’t beat that! All you need to do is cook the pasta,[ mar]inate (or coat if you don’t have time) the shrimp in pesto, saute the shrimp,[ make a simple creamy sauce for] the pasta, toss everything together, top the pasta[ with] shrim[ps], and finish[ with a sprinkle] of gr[ated par]mesan cheese and freshly chopped[ pars]ley[!]
[This] creamy wild garlic pesto shrimp pasta is packed with flavour[.] Perfect for lunch or dinner and can be ready in under 20 minutes!
Place all ingredients in a food processor and blitz until you reach the desired consistency. You can add more olive oil if needed.[
Mar]inate shrimp in wild[ garlic pest]o for 15-20 minutes. Or just coat in pesto if you don't have much time.
Cook pasta according to instructions on the pack. I add a little bit of olive oil and a pinch of salt to boiling water before adding pasta.
While pasta is cooking, cook the shrimps. Heat olive oil in a pan, then add shrimps and cook until shrimps are pink and round.
